AB  - The proceedings contain 13 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Skin Image Analysis and International Workshop on Computer-Aided Pelvic Imaging for Female Health. The topics include: Fitzpatrick Thresholding for Skin Image Segmentation; what Can We Learn from Inter-Annotator Variability in Skin Lesion Segmentation?; topology-Aware Deep Models for Skin Lesion Classification; Retrieval-Augmented VLMs for Multimodal Melanoma Diagnosis; Lightweight Dual-Task Framework for Semi-supervised Lesion Segmentation with Knowledge Distillation from SAM; UteroVAE: A Shape-Informed Variational Autoencoder for Uterine MRI Encoding in Adenomyosis, Fibroids, and Healthy Uteri; delineation Uncertainty from Clinician Ranges in Cervical Cancer Radiotherapy Planning; Diffusing the Blind Spot: Uterine MRI Synthesis with Diffusion Models; multi-step Segmentation of Pelvic Fractures: Handling Variable Fracture Counts Through Anatomical and Surface Analysis; Visionerves: Automatic and Reproducible Hybrid AI for Peripheral Nervous System Recognition Applied to Endometriosis Cases; A Prospective Dual-Modality Tool for Monitoring Uterine Peristalsis: Integrating Dynamic MRI and Electrohysterography.
