AB  - Neuroimmunology is a relatively new field which includes the diagnosis and treatment of immune-mediated disorders of the central and peripheral nervous systems. The primary diagnostic tools of this field such as neuroimaging modalities, including MRI, MR spectroscopy, perfusion imaging, etc. are essential and extensively utilized. In this chapter, we predominantly discuss the imaging morphology of central nervous system immunological disorders on MRI, and its various image sequences, for the purposes of diagnosis and treatment. There is no clear-cut classification of these disorders as the understanding of their etiopathogenesis and pathophysiology is still a growing field. We have attempted to categorize a comprehensive list of neuroimmunological disorders based on the pathological manifestations and provided a detailed breakdown of their imaging characteristics for most of these disorders. © 2023 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
