AB  - Chronic Inflammatory Demyelinating Polyneuropathy (CIDP) is a unique, progressive, and rare neurological condition that involves inflammation of peripheral nerves, demyelination of peripheral nerves, and causes muscle weakness, sensory impairment, and motor weakness. This requires early and accurate diagnosis to facilitate early intervention and avoidance of eventual disability. Nevertheless, traditional clinical assessments and electro diagnostics may show inconclusive or late results. This paper introduces a Deep Learning hybrid model incorporating Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) to automate the detection of CIDP with the following objectives: to increase the accuracy of CIDP diagnostics and minimise dependence on invasive tests. The model involves high-resolution MRI to see structural abnormalities in peripheral nerves. It is a fusion of Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) as a means of extracting features spatially, and Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs), namely, Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) schemas used to analyse sequential data. This mixed architecture enables this system to learn local patterns of texture and global contextual characteristics related with nerve damage related to CIDP. The diagnostic pipeline entails pre-processing of images, segmentation of nerve region, feature extraction, and classification. The model combines the spatial and temporal characteristics, and the combination enhances the model performance by classifying CIDP and other neuropathies substantially better than the single characteristics. The non-invasive, AI-based solution helps radiologists in making consistent and high-accuracy scans, thus improving the clinical decision-making and outcomes related to the diagnosis of a peripheral nerve disorder. © 2025, Scibulcom Ltd.. All rights reserved.
