AB  - The proceedings contain 24 papers. The topics discussed include: optical scatter imaging: a microscopic modality for the rapid morphological assay of living cells; near-infrared optical tomography: endoscopic imaging approach; fast optical response to electrical activation in peripheral nerves; diffuse optical fluorescence tomography using time-resolved data acquired in transmission; fluorescence optical tomography with a priori information; image reconstruction and evaluation of system performance for optical fluorescence tomography; cell segmentation for division rate estimation in computerized video time-lapse microscopy; structural a priori information in near-infrared optical tomography; combination of magnetic resonance imaging and diffuse optical spectroscopy to predict radiation response in the breast: an exploratory pilot study; and simultaneous monitoring of multiple contrast agents using a hybrid MR-DOT system.
