AB  - Soft-tissue masses in children may be inflammatory, reactive, or neoplastic. The distribution of soft-tissue tumors of the extremities in children is different fromthat in adults. Benign tumors aremuch more common than soft-tissue sarcomas. Vascular lesions are the most common benign tumors and rhabdomyosarcoma is the most common sarcoma in the pediatric population. The imaging characteristics often are nonspecific, and the diagnosis consists of putting together the clinical, imaging, and pathologic findings. The principles of diagnosis, clinical examination, imaging, and pathologic findings in some common pediatric soft-tissue tumors of the extremities are presented. Some of the more recent advances in imaging and pathology also are highlighted. 1940-7041 © 2013 Wolters Kluwer Health.
