AB  - Peripheral nerve disorders have been a Cinderella subspecialty for neurologists because of the limited treatment options and difficulties in obtaining a genetic diagnosis. In the last decade, there has been great progress in the management of patients with peripheral nerve disease. In this paper, we review a selection of diagnostic and therapeutic papers in this area published in the Journal of Neurology over the last 24 months. © 2013 Springer-Verlag Berlin Heidelberg.
